{:edb/db-before-t 2365 :edb/db-after-t 2366 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535678 50 #inst "2026-10-09T04:57:52.809Z" 13194139535678 true] [17592186179599 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360790 13194139535678 true] [17592186179599 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360797 13194139535678 true] [17592186179602 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360783 13194139535678 true] [17592186179668 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360770 13194139535678 true] [17592186180215 1017 #edb/ref 17592186179165 13194139535678 false] [17592186180215 1017 #edb/ref 17592186360777 13194139535678 true] [17592186180215 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535678 true] [17592186180215 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/assets/9fd222d255fd1a37f00cbe7c9abf6af0d0e3af92f9ac581591bb1062780e69fa.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $ABCA,$ shown in the diagram above, traversed in the **clockwise** direction?" 13194139535678 true] [17592186180215 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3704/Source/Images/q-76476.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral $∫_(C)F \\cdot dr$, where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $ABCA$, shown in the diagram above, traversed in the **clockwise** direction?" 13194139535678 false] [17592186180215 1145 "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed clockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC={-{C}_{1}}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {-{C}_{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{1}$ and $-{C}_{3}$ are the same paths as ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{3}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535678 true] [17592186360770 1017 #edb/ref 17592186360771 13194139535678 true] [17592186360770 1089 "q-125413" 13194139535678 true] [17592186360770 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535678 true] [17592186360770 1100 "Let $F(x,y,z)=2z\\,i+3x\\,j-4y\\,k$ and let $C$ be a path in ${R}^{3}.$ Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r?$" 13194139535678 true] [17592186360770 1113 #uuid "f6568490-f28b-51b2-8a83-ff4a151c3cd9" 13194139535678 true] [17592186360770 1145 "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\\,i+Q(x,y,z)\\,j+R(x,y,z)\\,k\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y+R(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}2z\\,\\text{d}x+3x\\,\\text{d}y-4y\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535678 true] [17592186360771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360772 13194139535678 true] [17592186360771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360773 13194139535678 true] [17592186360771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360774 13194139535678 true] [17592186360771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360775 13194139535678 true] [17592186360771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360776 13194139535678 true] [17592186360771 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535678 true] [17592186360771 1041 "selection" 13194139535678 true] [17592186360771 1104 #edb/ref 17592186360774 13194139535678 true] [17592186360771 1110 #uuid "d74d1e46-0258-52ef-8ff6-17e3b3961433" 13194139535678 true] [17592186360772 1034 "{\\int }_{C}-4y\\,\\text{d}x+2z\\,\\text{d}y+3x\\,\\text{d}z" 13194139535678 true] [17592186360772 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535678 true] [17592186360772 1111 #uuid "9a7020f5-a843-576e-b61f-411e39cd6c2b" 13194139535678 true] [17592186360773 1034 "{\\int }_{C}(2z+3x-4y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z" 13194139535678 true] [17592186360773 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535678 true] [17592186360773 1111 #uuid "be8